-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- West Bengal towns with an open ward map go on the report map as places.
--
-- The West Bengal AMRUT GIS ward maps (Ministry of Housing and Urban
-- Affairs; CC0 via india-geodata) cover 52 towns. Each becomes a place, the
-- same as a town sent in on add-town.html, so a report inside one of its
-- wards is filed under that town and ward (locate_place) instead of the
-- district. Rows are generated by tools/build-wb-towns.py.
--
-- A town someone has since fixed on add-town.html (community = true) keeps
-- its wards: re-running this never overwrites them.
-- Reports already filed under a district are re-checked once, so the ones
-- inside these wards move to their town.
--
-- Safe to re-run.
-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

begin;

-- ── Town rows: generated by tools/build-wb-towns.py, do not edit by hand ──
